# Single source of truth for the pinned dependencies every workflow installs.
#
# The versions used to be written out inline in three workflows, so they could drift apart
# without anything noticing: the lint gate and the required code-scanning check could analyse
# with different analyzers, and ConvertToSARIF was not pinned at all.
#
# Each workflow loads this file into $GITHUB_ENV immediately after checkout, then asserts
# every key arrived. Format is KEY=value, one per line; no quoting, no expansion.
#
# NOT covered here: `uses:` action SHAs. A workflow's `uses:` cannot reference a variable, so
# those stay written out in each file and have to be kept in step by hand. They are all
# SHA-pinned with the version in a trailing comment.

# The version the test estate is written against. Bump with CLAUDE.md.
PESTER_VERSION=6.1.0

# Deliberately NOT the version above: the compatibility gate proves a consumer on a DIFFERENT
# Pester can still gate on this module, which needs those versions installed alongside it.
#
# A list, not a single version, and one leg per MINOR across the whole supported range. A floor
# plus a latest was the first plan and is not enough: New-PesterConfiguration arrived in 5.1.0,
# which is invisible at both ends and fatal in between. Anything that lands mid-range has the same
# shape, so the middle is not interpolation.
#
# ONE RULE, no exceptions: the newest patch of every minor. The floor leg used to be 5.0.0 exactly,
# on the argument that the promised number should be the exercised one -- but a consumer does not
# install 5.0.0 when 5.0.4 exists, so it proved a version almost nobody runs, and it made the list
# the only one in this file needing an exemption a freshness watcher would have to be taught. A rule
# with one exception is two rules. Before any of this the gate ran 5.7.1 alone and the promise was
# never tested at all.
#
# Space-separated, like PSSA_PATHS. Each leg is about four seconds; the cost is the one-off
# install, and the module cache is keyed on this file.
PESTER_COMPAT_VERSIONS=5.0.4 5.1.1 5.2.2 5.3.3 5.4.1 5.5.0 5.6.1 5.7.1 5.8.0 5.9.1 6.0.1 6.1.0

# The PowerShell versions the module is proven on, newest patch of each supported minor. The
# manifest's PowerShellVersion is the floor consumers are told; this is what executes against it.
# CI runs whatever the runners ship, which is several minors newer, so without these legs the
# declared floor is a claim rather than a guarantee.
#
# The runners' own 7.6.x is covered by the ordinary suite and is deliberately not repeated here.
#
# 7.0 to 7.3 are end of support. Testing them is the honest consequence of promising 7.0; raising
# the floor is the alternative, and is a product decision rather than a technical one.
PS_COMPAT_VERSIONS=7.0.13 7.1.7 7.2.24 7.3.12 7.4.19 7.5.10

PSSA_VERSION=1.25.0
PSMUTANT_VERSION=0.4.0
CONVERTTOSARIF_VERSION=1.0.0

# What PSScriptAnalyzer looks at. Shared so the lint gate and the code-scanning check cannot
# disagree about scope: a finding in one and not the other is the least diagnosable kind of
# red build, and code scanning is a required check.
PSSA_PATHS=./src ./tests ./tools ./PSComplexity.psm1 ./PSComplexity.psd1
